# MMTSFM ablation sweep manifest — read by scripts/ablation_sweep.sh
#
# One row per registered ablation. The sweep script expands SEEDS into one run
# each, resolves the warm-start / scoring checkpoint from BASE, and packs the
# resulting jobs onto whole GPU nodes.
#
#   ID    | MODE  | STAGE | MODEL_CFG              | SEEDS    | BASE
#
# MODE   train = fit then test;  eval = score BASE's checkpoint only (no fit).
# BASE   checkpoint DIRECTORY under $CKPT_DIR, `{seed}` expanded per run.
#        train → ${CKPT_DIR}/<BASE>/best.ckpt is the weights-only warm start.
#        eval  → ${CKPT_DIR}/<BASE>/best.ckpt is the checkpoint under test.
#        A missing file is FATAL at submit time, on the login node, before any
#        allocation is spent — an ablation that silently starts from random init
#        produces a plausible-looking and meaningless arm.
#
# ⚠ VERIFY THE BASE COLUMN against what is actually on scratch before the first
#   submission. The s2c checkpoint directory name depends on which MODEL_CFG
#   produced it: `vision_chronos2_s2c` → uk_pv_s2c_s2c_s42, but
#   `vision_chronos2_timeselfattn` → uk_pv_s2c_selfattn_s42. knowledge/
#   running-ablations.md quotes the latter; slurm_curriculum.sh's worked example
#   derives the former. `ls $CKPT_DIR` settles it. This is the same unresolved
#   ambiguity as the s2b_wide fusion-mode question in running-ablations.md §0.
#
# Order matters: the sweep distributes jobs round-robin across packs, so rows
# are listed cheapest-decision-first (running-ablations.md §2).

# --- 1. eval-only negative controls: minutes each, can kill the paper ---------
# A09 (temporal shuffle) is NOT listed for s2c. It is a bit-exact no-op on
# `fusion_mode: future_query` — _build_visual_kv emits one flat, position-free
# key set attended under an all-zero kv_mask — so on_test_start REFUSES it. A09i
# is that null recorded deliberately as an ARCHITECTURAL claim; one seed is
# enough because the output equals the plain s2c test JSON exactly, for every
# seed, by construction. See configs/ablation/A09.yaml.
# RETIRED 2026-09-07 (s2b/s2c out of scope): A09i| eval  | s2c | vision_chronos2_s2c        | 42       | uk_pv_s2c_s2c_s{seed}
# A10 needs data.shuffle_test=true (set in its own config): the protocol test
# loader is series-major, so an ordered batch is ONE plant and no sample can be
# handed a DIFFERENT plant's sky.
# RETIRED 2026-09-07 (s2b/s2c out of scope): A10 | eval  | s2c | vision_chronos2_s2c        | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s2c_s2c_s{seed}
# A10b = same plant, sky one horizon stale. This is what the pre-2026-09 runs
# labelled A10 actually measured; it separates "reads THIS sky" from "reads A
# sky from this site", which is the claim the 4x4 grid has to support.
# RETIRED 2026-09-07 (s2b/s2c out of scope): A10b| eval  | s2c | vision_chronos2_s2c        | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s2c_s2c_s{seed}
# A09 on s2a is the negative control's own control: if late fusion degrades as
# much as s2c under shuffling, the control measures something other than motion.
# It is ALSO the only arm where A09 is falsifiable at all — and only if that arm
# ran with n_visual_context_steps > 1. At 1 the LatentSummarizer is a set
# function over the token bag and on_test_start refuses it for that reason too.
# DISABLED 2026-09-01: `uk_pv_s2a_base_s{42,43,44}` do not exist on scratch — the
# submit-time check refused all six rows. `_base_` assumes MODEL_CFG
# `vision_chronos2` produced the s2a arm, but wave 1 ran grassmann and
# timeselfattn, so the arm on disk is `uk_pv_s2a` (canonical grassmann@42, no
# suffix), `uk_pv_s2a_grassmann_s{43,44}` or `uk_pv_s2a_selfattn_s{seed}`.
# Restore with the name `ls $CKPT_DIR | grep s2a` reports, and set MODEL_CFG to
# the config that produced it — the two must agree or the control scores one arm
# while claiming to be the late-fusion counterpart of another. Check that arm's
# vision_cfg.n_visual_context_steps before restoring the A09 row.
# A09 | eval  | s2a | <MODEL_CFG>              | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s2a<SUFFIX>
# A10 | eval  | s2a | <MODEL_CFG>              | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s2a<SUFFIX>

# --- 2. the attribution pair: grid vs decoder granularity --------------------
# RETIRED 2026-09-07 (s2b/s2c out of scope): A17 | train | s2c | vision_chronos2_s2c        | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed}
# RETIRED 2026-09-07 (s2b/s2c out of scope): A22 | train | s2c | vision_chronos2_s2c        | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed}
# A29 is the third leg: A17/A22 split grid vs decoder INSIDE s2c, A29 splits the
# spatially resolved payload from the forecast-side query by giving s2b s2c's exact
# 4x4x4 payload through a widened LatentSummarizer. STAGE is s2b (interleaved) but
# MODEL_CFG is s2c's, so everything except the fusion route is held fixed against
# A16. See knowledge/ablations.md §2.2.2.
# RETIRED 2026-09-07 (s2b/s2c out of scope): A29 | train | s2b | vision_chronos2_s2c        | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed}

# --- 3. is A01's negative result clean? -------------------------------------
