# A17 comes back positive, and its KV token count is ~784/sample against s2c's 64
# — it needs its own BATCH_SIZE. Uncomment and set SWEEP_BATCH once A17 lands.
# A21 | train | s2c | vision_chronos2_s2c      | 42       | uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed}


# =============================================================================
# WAVE 3 — s2d (A30 / interleaved_raw). The only arms in scope for the paper.
# =============================================================================
# Everything above this line is the s2b/s2c wave and is commented out: those
# arms answer questions about a destination the project no longer has. Rows
# below are ordered by decision value per GPU-hour — cheapest kill first, so an
# early null stops the wave instead of being discovered after 30 node-hours.
#
# BASE, verified against `ls $CKPT_DIR`:
#   uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed}  — the s1 fine-tune every s2* arm warm-starts from
#   uk_pv_s2d_s2d_s{seed}      — the shipped s2d checkpoint (MODEL_CFG
#                                vision_chronos2_s2d → `_s2d_` infix, per the
#                                naming rule in the ⚠ note above)

# --- 1. eval-only: minutes, and A38 can retire ticket 42 on its own ----------
# A38 swaps EVS's novelty rule for uniform random ON THE TRAINED s2d WEIGHTS.
# Parameter-free (tests/test_s2d_component_ablations.py asserts the state_dicts
# match), so no fit is needed to ask whether the SELECTION RULE matters at
# inference. Escalate to A38t only if ramp NMAE moves by more than the seed
# floor 0.0011.
A38 | eval  | s2d | vision_chronos2_s2d        | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s2d_s2d_s{seed}

# --- 2. cheap config-only trains: one knob, no new code ----------------------
# A39 — n_unfreeze_encoder_blocks=0, i.e. the "frozen TSFM" the writeup already
# claims twice. Ticket 43. The prose fix lands regardless; this row decides
# whether the strong claim is also TRUE.
A39 | train | s2d | vision_chronos2_s2d        | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed}
# A43 — late_raw. s2d's payload at s2b's integer position: isolates H2
# (fractional sub-patch placement) with one knob. Ticket 28.
A43 | train | s2d | vision_chronos2_s2d        | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed}
# A37 — avg pooling instead of pixel shuffle. Isolates H1 (sub-cell detail)
# with token count held fixed. Ticket 41. proj[0].in_features changes, so this
# CANNOT warm-start from s2d — s1 base is mandatory, not a convenience.
A37 | train | s2d | vision_chronos2_s2d        | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed}

# --- 3. the expensive one: two chained arms, both seeds-complete -------------
# A36 — history-only covariates (ticket 40). The s2d arm MUST warm-start from
# the A36 s1 arm, not from the existing all-covariate s1, or the comparison
# inherits an optimum found under the covariates it is meant to remove. That
# dependency is why these are two rows and why the second cannot be submitted
# until the first has written its checkpoints.
# A36s1 is NOT submittable through this sweep and is commented out on purpose:
# the BASE column is a mandatory, submit-time-checked checkpoint file, and an s1
# arm starts from the PRETRAINED Chronos-2, not from a checkpoint on scratch.
# Launch it with slurm_curriculum.sh, once per seed:
#   START_STAGE=s1 END_STAGE=s1 SEED=<42|43|44> \
#   MODEL_CFG=vision_chronos2_a36 EXTRA_OVERRIDES="+ablation=A36s1" \
#   bash scripts/slurm_curriculum.sh
# MODEL_CFG is vision_chronos2_a36, NOT vision_chronos2_timeselfattn, even though
# the two compose to an identical model: slurm_curriculum.sh derives the
# checkpoint dir and the results tag from MODEL_CFG, so timeselfattn would write
# straight into uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed} and destroy the s1 that A37/A39/A43
# warm-start from. Listed here so the wave is readable in one place.
# A36s1 | train | s1  | vision_chronos2_a36     | 42,43,44 | <pretrained Chronos-2>
# A36s2d BASE is A36s1's output directory — uk_pv_s1_a36_s{seed}, the name
# variant_slug() gives that MODEL_CFG. Submit only after A36s1 completes; the
# manifest's submit-time existence check will refuse it otherwise, which is the
# intended behaviour rather than a failure.
A36s2d| train | s2d | vision_chronos2_s2d       | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s1_a36_s{seed}

# --- 4. conditional: only if A38's eval moves ramp NMAE > 0.0011 -------------
# A38t | train | s2d | vision_chronos2_s2d      | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed}
